  "text": "To find the sum of all integer bases \\( b > 9 \\) for which \\( 17_b \\) is a divisor of \\( 97_b \\), we need to first convert these numbers from base \\( b \\) to base 10 and then check the divisibility condition.\n\n1. **Convert \\( 17_b \\) and \\( 97_b \\) to base 10:**\n   - \\( 17_b = 1 \\cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \\)\n   - \\( 97_b = 9 \\cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \\)\n\n2. **Check the divisibility condition:**\n   - For \\( 17_b \\) to be a divisor of \\( 97_b \\), \\( b + 7 \\) must divide \\( 9b + 7 \\).\n   - This means that there exists an integer \\( k \\) such that \\( 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \\).\n\n3. **Solve for \\( b \\):**\n   - Rearrange the equation: \\( 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \\)\n   - Expand and rearrange: \\( 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \\)\n   - Collect terms involving \\( b \\): \\( 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \\)\n   - Factor out \\( b \\): \\( b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \\)\n   - Solve for \\( b \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \\)\n\n4. **Find integer solutions for \\( b \\):**\n   - We need \\( b \\) to be an integer greater than 9.\n   - Check possible values of \\( k \\) that make \\( b \\) an integer:\n     - For \\( k = 10 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(10 - 1)}{9 - 10} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 9}{-1} = -63 \\) (not valid)\n     - For \\( k = 9 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(9 - 1)}{9 - 9} \\) (undefined)\n     - For \\( k = 8 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(8 - 1)}{9 - 8} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 7}{1} = 49 \\) (valid)\n     - For \\( k = 7 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(7 - 1)}{9 - 7} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 6}{2} = 21 \\) (valid)\n     - For \\( k = 6 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(6 - 1)}{9 - 6} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 5}{3} \\) (not an integer)\n     - For \\( k = 5 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(5 - 1)}{9 - 5} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 4}{4} = 7 \\) (not valid since \\( b > 9 \\))\n     - For \\( k = 4 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(4 - 1)}{9 - 4} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 3}{5} \\) (not an integer)\n     - For \\( k = 3 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(3 - 1)}{9 - 3} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 2}{6} = \\frac{7}{3} \\) (not an integer)\n     - For \\( k = 2 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(2 - 1)}{9 - 2} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 1}{7} = 1 \\) (not valid since \\( b > 9 \\))\n     - For \\( k = 1 \\): \\( b = \\frac{7(1 - 1)}{9 - 1} = 0 \\) (not valid)\n\n5. **Sum the valid bases:**\n   - The valid bases are \\( b = 21 \\) and \\( b = 49 \\).\n   - Sum: \\( 21 + 49 = 70 \\)\n\nTherefore, the sum of all integer bases \\( b > 9 \\) for which \\( 17_b \\) is a divisor of \\( 97_b \\) is \\(\\boxed{70}\\).",
